thing about him being not nice. Rule 5 says all smart things are white. So if Gary is smart, he is white. But rule 7 says if something is smart and not rough, then it is quiet. If Gary is smart and not rough, then he is quiet. But if Gary is rough, then from rule 1, he is quiet. Wait, perhaps I'm getting confused.\n\nLet me try to summarize:\n\n- Gary is red and white.\n- From rule 2: All white things are rough, so Gary is rough.\n- From rule 3: If something is rough, then it is red. So Gary is red, which is consistent.\n- From rule 1: If Gary is red and white, then he is quiet. So Gary is quiet.\n- Therefore, the statement \"Gary is not quiet\" is false.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Gary is not quiet\" is false because Gary is both red and white, which according to rule 1, makes him quiet. Therefore, Gary is actually quiet.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
